# =============================================
# Secure Docker Blueprint – stacks on this host
# =============================================
# Copy to `stacks` (ignored by Git) and keep one stack path per line.
# `scripts/stacks.sh apply` checks out exactly these paths; `scripts/stacks.sh
# update <tag>` previews and takes a release for them.
#
# `scripts` and `docs/standards` are always checked out and need no line.
# Removing a line removes the stack from this host; apply refuses while the
# stack still has .env, .secrets/, volumes/ or other local files.
# =============================================

core/traefik
core/crowdsec
apps/whoami

# Examples — remove the # to add a stack:
# apps/vaultwarden
# apps/nextcloud
# backup/borgmatic
# monitoring/uptime-kuma
